<<~ ahu #/overview>>

!! Overview

TW5 deserializes tiddler content by content-type. The deserializer for `text/memetic-wikitext` declares `module-type: tiddlerdeserializer`; TW5's native module loader collects it at boot into `$tw.modules.types.tiddlerdeserializer`, keyed by content-type. The compiled CJS exports the function under its content-type key — `exports["text/memetic-wikitext"] = memeticWikitextDeserializer` — so TW5 reaches it through the same registry `$tw.wiki.deserializeTiddlers` reads. When TW5 meets a tiddler of this type, it calls the collected function to split the raw carrier text into one parent tiddler and N ahu child slot tiddlers — the same structural split the disk projector performs on the Node side.

The canonical source rests at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/modules/deserializer`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/split-model>>

!! Split Model

The entry `memeticWikitextDeserializer(text, fields)` streams the raw text through `MemeStreamParser` (single-meme, multi-meme, and partial carriers all flow), then routes each carrier-close event through `splitMemeToTiddlers` → `splitRecursive`. The root tiddler reads its complete authorial TOML block immediately after STX; each `<<~ ahu #/slot>>` or `<<fragment #/slot>>` block becomes a child tiddler holding its body bytes authoritatively, the parent keeping a `<<~ kahea ahu #/slot>>` reference in its place. Legacy pre-STX root metadata is recoverable only with a visible diagnostic; the emitter never recreates it. Transport prologue/postamble may ride records of their own, while scalar carriage — `$slot`, `$fragment-parent`, `$carrier-soh` — stays on fields (see lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext-framing#/the-carriage). The STX–ETX check covers root TOML and all authored content.

A split failure never truncates: `safeSplitMeme` falls back to one verbatim tiddler flagged `lar_parse_degraded`, and grades the parse via `parseMemeText().failures` into `lar_parse_failures` — degradation surfaces legibly rather than dropping bytes.

Parse warnings ride a synthesised `$:/lararium/parse-warning/<slug>` tiddler (`PARSE_WARNING_TAG`). The `deserializeCarrier(text, fields)` wrapper reads that same channel and returns `{ records, diagnostics }` on the shared `MemeDiagnostic` contract, so a gate reads a grade rather than sniffing a title.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/module-collection>>

!! The Module Rides the Native Registry

The deserializer travels as a plugin tiddler — TS source compiled to a CJS module tiddler carrying `module-type: tiddlerdeserializer`. TW5 collects every such module by type at boot; the content-type key on the export binds the function to `text/memetic-wikitext` with no imperative property assignment and no closure over a live wiki class. Disk ingest and store load converge on the exact registry: `$tw.wiki.deserializeTiddlers` dispatches by content-type into the collected set.

The paired `carrier-filetype` startup module registers `.mem` as `text/memetic-wikitext` through `$tw.config.fileExtensionInfo`, so drag-and-drop, the import dialog, and the filesystem adaptor route as one. ''One extension, one type'' — the extension answers the only question a content sniff could ask, and a malformed carrier reaches the carrier reader (which names the fault) rather than a router that would reclassify it away from its own diagnostic.

<<~/ahu>>

